# sweep: articles
# Three web articles clipped from saved pages sit in the card's Articles
# folder beside one book. They get a shelf of their own, a list with each
# one's site and when it arrived, and the Library shelf keeps to the books.
wait-for 3 unread
expect Library
expect 1 book
clean
shot books-articles-home
tap Articles
wait-for The Harbour Gazette
expect Longform Monthly
expect Notes from the Slipway
expect Sync
expect-missing A Walk by the River
clean
shot books-articles-shelf
# An article opens in the shared reader like any book, and Back returns to
# the shelf it was opened from.
tap Harbour wall to be rebuilt after winter storms
wait-for Saved from
clean
shot books-article-open
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Sync
expect Harbour wall to be rebuilt after winter storms
# Archive, from the row's menu, puts an article away under Archived, and
# Move back to Articles brings it back. Rows are named by their place: the
# last page clipped is the newest and the first row.
tap-id article-menu-0
wait-for Archive
clean
shot books-article-menu
tap Archive
wait-for Archived
expect-missing The last lighthouse keepers
tap Archived
wait-for The last lighthouse keepers
expect Archived articles
clean
shot books-articles-archived
tap-id article-menu-0
wait-for Move back to Articles
tap Move back to Articles
wait-for No archived articles
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Sync
expect The last lighthouse keepers
expect-missing Archived
# Delete asks first. Keep article leaves it on the shelf; Delete article
# takes it off the reader.
tap-id article-menu-2
wait-for Delete
tap Delete
wait-for Delete this article?
clean
shot books-article-delete
tap Keep article
wait-for Measuring tide heights with a pressure sensor
tap-id article-menu-2
wait-for Delete
tap Delete
wait-for Delete this article?
tap Delete article
wait-for Sync
wait-idle
expect-missing Measuring tide heights with a pressure sensor
expect Harbour wall to be rebuilt after winter storms
clean
shot books-articles-after-delete
